load @cluesurf/form/code/structure/set
  find set

# An interaction net: a model of computation by local graph rewriting, where agents joined at ports rewrite two at a
# time by fixed interaction rules, strongly confluent so the order of rewrites never changes the result. Interaction
# nets are inherently parallel and LINEAR (each wire is used exactly once), which is exactly the linear multiplicity of
# the kernel and exactly the discipline the substrate runs on. They are the runtime the vibe language compiles to. The
# form carries the set of agents; the ports and interaction rules are the net.
form interaction-net
  link agents, like set
